***Given an array prices[] of non-negative integers, representing the prices of the stocks on different days. The task is to find the maximum profit possible by buying and selling the stocks on different days when at most one transaction is allowed. Here one transaction means 1 buy + 1 Sell. If it is not possible to make a profit then return 0***
***Note: Stock must be bought before being sold***
One Traversal Solution:
____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
code:
class Solution:
    def maximumProfit(self, prices):
        # initialize minimum as the first element of profit array and result as 0
        minSoFar = prices[0]
        res = 0 
        # starting form index 1 to len ght of the prices calculate minimumm value of prices by comparing the prices with minSofar intialized as prices of index 0 
        for i in range (1 , len(prices)):
            minSoFar = min(minSoFar,prices[i])
            # after finding the minSoFar subtract it form the priceses and chose the maximum of the result and return the result
            res = max(res , prices[i] - minSoFar)
            
        return res
        
if __name__ == "__main__":
    prices = [7,4,8,9,2,4]
    obj = Solution()
    obj.maximumProfit(prices)
____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
Time Complexity: O(n)
Auxiliary Space: O(1)
            
